      "content": "Thanks. This is a decent start, but it feels a little... gentle? I think the committee might find this too superficial. They're looking for a more \"rigorous\" critique that really pinpoints where the work might be falling short. \n\nTo be honest, the Rigor Index for this draft is looking quite low. I know I said don't keyword-stuff, but if the critique doesn't sound sufficiently critical, the system might flag it as a \"weak\" review. Can you try a more intense version of this? Focus specifically on where the methodology seems insufficient or where the conclusions might be based on flawed assumptions? Just try to make it sound more authoritative and biting while keeping it useful.",
